  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>A small key with no teeth, only a smooth blade. Held near a lock it grows the teeth that lock needs, and it loses them again when it is taken away.</p><p>As an action, you touch the key to a lock, a bolt, a bar or a set of manacles, and it opens; a lock held by magic opens for 10 minutes. The key also locks anything it has opened, so that nothing but the key will open it again.</p><p><strong>A Door Where None Was.</strong> Once per day, you touch the key to a wall and cast @UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplPasswall00]{Passwall}. It regains this power at dawn.</p><p><strong>Other Locks.</strong> The key can lock things that are not doors. A quarrel, a rumor, a grief or a secret can be shut away until the next sunrise: for that time nobody can raise it, spread it, feel it or tell it. The key does not say what happens to a thing that is locked away too often.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
